# What ships inside an application's vendor/ directory.
#
# example/ is a whole generated Laravel app plus its stubs, and logo.png is
# over a megabyte. Neither has any business being downloaded by every project
# that installs this package.
#
# composer.lock is deliberately absent from this list: it is gitignored, so it
# is not in the repository and cannot be in the archive. A line for it here
# would claim to exclude something that never shipped.
#
# AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md are written for someone changing this package,
# not for someone using it.
#
# tests/ deliberately DOES ship. docs/verifying.md tells operators to run
# `php vendor/innerloop-dev/lightspeed/tests/integration/...` against their own
# running server, and a check you cannot run where the problem is happening is
# not much of a check.
#
# deploy/ deliberately ships too, for the same reason at one remove: docs/ ships,
# and docs/PRODUCTION.md and docs/configuration.md point operators at
# `../deploy/nginx` and `../deploy/systemd` by relative path. Ignoring three
# small text files would turn those links into dead ends for anyone reading the
# docs where they installed them.

example/           export-ignore
logo.png           export-ignore
.github/           export-ignore
.gitattributes     export-ignore
.gitignore         export-ignore
phpunit.xml        export-ignore
AGENTS.md          export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md    export-ignore
